values ('c4d5e6f7-9a0b-4c54-9d34-4e5f6a7b8c44', 'social-work-practice-with-communities-and-organizations', 'Social Work Practice with Communities and Organizations', 'This course prepares BSW students for ethical, justice-centered generalist practice with communities and organizations. Students learn to engage constituencies, assess assets and power, organize collective action, build coalitions, analyze policy, develop programs, understand organizations, support change, manage resources, evaluate results, and communicate strategically. A community-engaged project integrates the full macro-practice cycle.');

